--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SignalsWorkspacePage.tsx is the unified /signals workspace — a thin orchestrator
that composes the seven shared telemetry surfaces (SignalCategoryTree,
SignalChartPanel, SignalStatsPanel, SignalHistoryTable, LiveSignalTail,
SignalCompareControls, SignalDiffTable) around two mutually-exclusive Live /
Compare mode toggles, leaving a sensible Historical default. It lifts the
selection + mode out of those children so a headline strip of four StatCards
(Selected / Mode / Live-rate / Pinned-signals) and the Run/Live gating read from
one source of truth, and it owns four data sources: useSignals (the available
catalog), usePinned + useTogglePin (the signal-diff pin store), and
useSignalDiffServer (the two-snapshot diff). The parity manifest records
requiredCount=58: 11 panels (the 4 headline StatCards, the toolbar GlassPanel5,
the 4 compare StatCards Changed/Visible/Pinned/Window-span, the diff GlassPanel10,
and the historical empty GlassPanel11), 4 data states, and 43 strings.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION (no placeholders, ADR-011; no delegation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The shared A3 telemetry feature views already exist as native Compose surfaces
(io.teslasync.android.featureviews.{signalcomparecontrols,signaldifftable,
signalstatspanel,signalchartpanel,signalhistorytable,livesignaltail}) and own
their own loading / empty / error+retry / stale / content states. This page is
their host + orchestrator: it sets the PageContainer-equivalent header (title +
subtitle + VehicleSelect action + live-connection badge + share), reads the four
manifest feeds through a page ViewModel bound to the shared P1/S8 holders, lifts
the selection + mode, and renders the web tree — never re-implementing the shared
surfaces (DRY, ADR-006). Mirrors the sibling telemetry/SignalGapDetectorPage and
driving/RegenEfficiencyPage hosts (which build a page-local Http*Repository
because the Android DI graph wires no domain store yet).

New files (package io.teslasync.android.telemetry.signalsworkspace):
  - SignalsWorkspacePageModel.kt   Registration(ROUTE_ID signalsWorkspace,
                                   WEB_PATH /signals, SLUG SignalsWorkspacePage,
                                   DEFAULT_PER_PAGE, LIVE_TAIL_MAX) + WorkspaceMode
                                   {Historical,Live,Compare} + the pure derivations
                                   the page lifts out of the children:
                                   pinnedSignalNames (web pinnedSignals),
                                   filterDiffRows/diffFilterActive (web
                                   diffFilteredRows), windowSpanSeconds (web
                                   windowSpan), mergeHistoryRows/toChartRows/
                                   toStats/paginateRows (web chartData /
                                   historicalStats / paginatedRows), and the
                                   one PII-safe view.opened recorder (P1/S11).
  - SignalsWorkspacePageViewModel.kt  Binds SelectedVehicleStore (web
                                   useSelectedVehicle, self-healed to first
                                   vehicle), a page-local TelemetryStore over the
                                   injected TelemetryRepository, and the shared
                                   PinnedStore. Exposes UiState projections for
                                   signals (useSignals), pinned (usePinned), the
                                   on-demand diffState (useSignalDiffServer) and
                                   historyState (the manual-Run multi-signal
                                   useQuery, one /history read per selected signal
                                   adapted + folded), plus togglePin
                                   (useTogglePin). Extends BaseFeedViewModel.
  - SignalsWorkspacePage.kt        Stateful entry SignalsWorkspacePage(
                                   telemetryRepository, logger): records
                                   view.opened, builds the VM via viewModel(
                                   key=SLUG, factory=...), collects the four feeds
                                   + the live-connection snapshot; stateless
                                   SignalsWorkspacePageContent owns the ephemeral
                                   URL-equivalent state (lifted selection, mode,
                                   range, per-page, compare window+filter, chart
                                   layout, bulk selection) and renders
                                   WorkspaceHeader, HeadlineStatStrip,
                                   AddSignalsAccordion, WorkspaceToolbar, and the
                                   active mode's CompareSection or
                                   HistoricalLiveSection + WorkspaceFooter.
  - SignalsWorkspacePageHost.kt    SignalsWorkspaceRoute() resolves
                                   LocalDataContainer, builds a page-local
                                   HttpTelemetryRepository(container.api,
                                   container.cacheStore); SignalsWorkspacePageHost
                                   .register() -> PageHosts.register(
                                   "signalsWorkspace"). Idempotent.

