Honest disclosures (no red-as-green, no silent drift):
  - The "Add signals" catalog is a searchable Checkbox selector over the in-scope
    useSignals feed, lifting the selection into the page (the web
    SignalCategoryTree onChange contract) so the headline "Selected" StatCard, the
    Run/Live gating and the diff signalsCsv read one source of truth. The shared
    SignalCategoryTree feature view encapsulates its selection internally and so
    is not embedded here.
  - The Live-rate StatCard shows the merged live signal count for the selected
    vehicle while streaming and the em-dash otherwise (web isLive ? rate : "—");
    the authoritative per-second tail rate is rendered by the embedded
    LiveSignalTail. The live-connection badge reads the shared LiveSessionStore.
  - Time Range reuses the shared TIME_RANGE_PRESETS hour tokens (1h/6h/24h/7d/30d)
    rather than a date-range picker; the web RangePicker is itself preset-driven.
  - The diff bulk "Copy CSV" / "Add as alert rule" actions export to the system
    clipboard (there is no in-app file-download or cross-route navigator seam on
    the page-host content), while Pin/Unpin call the real useTogglePin mutation.
  - SavedViewMenu (a saved-views data source outside this unit's four manifest
    sources) is not wired; the share CopyButton covers the header permalink action.
  - i18n: signalsWorkspace.* / help.signal.live.aria are NOT in the web canonical
    en.json (the web resolves them from inline t() fallback defaults); the
    generator sources from web/src/i18n and cascades to apple/windows, both
    outside this artifact's allowed files, so the exact inline-default values are
    inserted into res/values*/strings.xml (the artifact's allowed string catalog).
    MissingTranslation/ExtraTranslation are disabled in the app lint config.

